tt-bio-demo (0.6.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Affinity questions: the booth now answers a real question about two
    molecules together -- does this ligand bind this protein -- with
    tt-bio's nesso1 model on a chip held in reserve for it. The answer is
    the model's own score plus a highlight of the residues nearest the
    ligand, never a number alone. Off by default (opt in with
    --questions, or live with Ctrl+A); a booth left alone cycles through
    the three shipped questions on its own, or a visitor taps one from
    the gallery.
  * The quad's own fourth cell -- the one Q&A's chip reservation leaves
    empty on a 4-chip booth -- shows the question and its answer at booth
    scale, instead of sitting blank next to the small rail panel.
  * A packaged (.deb / systemd) install could enumerate zero fold
    targets, and the documented way to enable Q&A on that install path
    did not reach the daemon at all; both fixed, and verified against a
    real install on a QB2-factory-layout image, not only unit tests.
  * The `?` help card and the gallery's own caption are shorter and no
    longer claim a hardcoded chip count that Q&A's chip reservation can
    make false.
  * The docs site's molecule count and model-family count are corrected:
    "six molecules" had been stale since yeast tRNA-Phe joined the
    playlist several releases ago and was never caught, and the model
    count now matches the fourteen families the site's own runs-today
    table already listed.

